//! The `caret-color` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property sets the color
//! of the insertion caret, sometimes referred to as the text input cursor. This is the visible
//! marker appearing at the insertion point where the next character typed will be added or where the
//! next character deleted will be removed.
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Generally resolves to
//! [`currentColor`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/color_value#currentcolor_keyword),
//! the `color` of the text that will be modified.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <color> [auto | <color>]?
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui-4/#propdef-caret-color
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/caret-color
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

